From 1b078102159f4e73b5b47bb117ded8f75998cb48 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:33:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: Allow delegated cgroup v2 thread scheduling

Permit App domains and the WebView zygote's pre-transition child
to use their existing delegated thread scheduling files. Keep cgroup v1
access forbidden for Apps and retain DAC ownership of process controls
and ancestor resource budgets.
Match the existing cgroup MLS object classification so categorized Apps
can use those TE permissions under enforcing SELinux. Allow only the
child zygotes' self-created startup pipes and system_server's FD use and
write, so cgroup delegation can finish before specialization continues.
Let the root zygote inspect its waiting descendants before delegating their
scheduling files, and let App zygote children read that scheduling metadata.
Keep system_server's original capability set. Permit installd to read
the cgroup v2 metadata needed to apply its dex2oat scheduling profile.

Signed-off-by: 5656565566 <contact@home56.top>
---
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/app.te             | 4 ++++
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/app_neverallows.te | 3 ++-
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/app_zygote.te      | 7 +++++++
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/priv_app.te        | 3 ++-
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/system_server.te   | 4 ++++
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/webview_zygote.te  | 7 +++++++
 prebuilts/api/31.0/private/zygote.te          | 5 +++++
 prebuilts/api/31.0/public/file.te             | 2 +-
